FROM python:3.12.14-slim-trixie@sha256:f77ac9e44ae96ef2c90b8053ea08c31f8be030f824196b0ae4db6d462c84e51f
WORKDIR /app

# Security gate: the pinned base digest can lag Debian point releases. Apply
# repository security updates so the release image carries patched system
# packages (checked by the container-image-scan CI job).
RUN apt-get update \
    && apt-get upgrade -y \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# Keep the network-facing process on a fixed unprivileged service account.
# The image-owned local-storage directory is writable by the same account.
RUN groupadd -g 10001 app && useradd -m -u 10001 -g 10001 -s /bin/bash app && \
    mkdir -p /app/storage && \
    chown -R app:app /app

COPY backend/requirements.txt ./requirements.txt
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt

# Token accounting must not depend on a first-request network download.
ENV DATA_GYM_CACHE_DIR=/opt/lorevia/tiktoken
RUN mkdir -p "$DATA_GYM_CACHE_DIR" \
    && python -c "import tiktoken; tiktoken.encoding_for_model('gpt-4o-mini')" \
    && chmod -R a=rX "$DATA_GYM_CACHE_DIR"

# The optional spaCy model has a tested conservative fallback, so builders may
# opt into the larger language asset without making it a release prerequisite.
ARG PREFETCH_SPACY_MODEL=0
RUN if [ "$PREFETCH_SPACY_MODEL" = "1" ]; then \
        python -m spacy download en_core_web_sm; \
    fi

COPY backend/ .
RUN chmod +x start.sh worker-start.sh && chown -R app:app /app

ARG RELEASE_SHA=unknown
ENV RELEASE_SHA=$RELEASE_SHA
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.revision=$RELEASE_SHA

EXPOSE 8000
USER 10001:10001
ENTRYPOINT ["./worker-start.sh"]
CMD ["./start.sh"]
